            <ArticleTitle>Anticancer Potential of Thiazole Derivatives: A Retrospective Review.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2174/1389557517666171123211321</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Thiazole nucleus is one of the most important and well-known heterocyclic nuclei that possesses almost all types of biological activities. Thiazole compounds play an important role in anticancer drug development as they have shown excellent results through different mechanism of action. A number of thiazole derivatives have been reported till date for their anticancer activity. The present review is complementary to earlier reviews and aims to review the work reported on the anticancer activity of thiazole derivatives from year 2000 to the beginning of 2016. Their mechanism of action and possible structure activity relationship has also been discussed.</AbstractText>
